            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I came to allrecipes looking specifically for a meatball recipe for a slow cooker. Little did I know I would find a recipe so easy and so tasty! THANKS. It's a big hit with my friends!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it using Sweet Baby Rays, added garlic, pineapple, red/yellow bell peppers, grape jelly, crushed/cut up chipotle peppers in adobo sauce and served it over rice. *HUGE* hit with my kid and bf.",
            "datePublished": "2024-08-13T18:30:03.695Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tina Marie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great and easy recipe. I made it for a Super Bowl party. I used 3 different BBQ sauces: Regular KC Masterpiece, KC Masterpiece Hickory Brown Sugar, and Gates BBQ sauce, and without the ketchup. Another way to do this is to cook the meatballs by themselves in the oven until hot and then put in the slow cooker with the BBQ sauces and keep warm until served.",
            "datePublished": "2009-01-29T10:38:45.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mrmanning"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made my own meatballs instead of using frozen ones, so the cook time was a little longer (3.5 hours). These are great every time, and always seem to be the first thing that disappears when company comes over. Great for the beginner, or those strapped for time. Add 2 table spoons of raspberry jam and a touch of honey for enhanced sweetness. Very good.",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-08T16:53:29.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bing"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I opted to do this on the stove for time purposes. I didn't have enough BBQ sauce so I added about 1/4 French dressing. Kids ages 2&amp;7 gobbled it up. Served over white rice per someone else's suggestion.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-13T21:31:21.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "raisinpickle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "AMAZING!!!! I totally lied and said I made this from scratch!!! ;) This is a really amazing foundation for your own special customized bbq meatball recipe. I doubled the ingredients stated in the recipe and I also put my own twist on it. I think the brand of sauce is super important...I used Original Sweet Baby Ray's and Publix brand frozen meatballs...I also added an 8oz. can of crushed pineapple (un-drained), a tablespoon of ground cayenne pepper, and 1 teaspoon of garlic powder...AMAZING!! HUGE hit! The guys were licking their plates!... yum!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-06T13:42:12.660Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JENNIFER72_00"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for my husband and he really liked it. I didn't use a slow cooker but instead let the meatballs simmer in a pot on the stove for 1 hour. I served them over white rice. Very easy.",
            "datePublished": "2006-05-19T09:46:54.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dani Lee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this was a delicious and easy way to whip up some meatballs. I used Simeks Meatballs, Jack Daniels Honey Smokehouse BBQ Sauce (which has a little smokey flavor to it) and added the Ketchup and some Worcestershire Sauce and a sprinkle of Garlic Salt. Delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-03T16:12:20.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marika Clarke Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty!! we had someone in our group very sensitive to beef so we used turkey meatballs and it was great! I also use chili sauce instead of ketchup. super easy recipe and great for",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-24T13:28:44.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FluffyPulp7593"
            },
